<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Tietmeyer says Amsterdam EU deal &quot;temporary&quot;.</title>
<headline>Tietmeyer says Amsterdam EU deal &quot;temporary&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer said on Friday Europe was at a crossroads on integration and that further agreement on a way forward would be necessary.</p>
<p>Speaking in Prague, Tietmeyer said: &quot;An institutional reform would lend greater definition to the union. The results of the Amsterdam summit are in this case only temporary and do not offer a sufficiently long-term solution.&quot;  </p>
<p>European leaders in Amsterdam agreed a revised treaty aimed at paving the way for enlargement of the European Union, but left open many questions needed for reform of European instititutions.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
